  "predictive_services_discussion": "Widespread elevated to critical conditions will persist across southern portions of the Great Basin, as well as the Southwest and central Rockies today. Southwest winds 15-30 mph with gusts 30-45 mph are expected across these areas with the highest winds expected across the central Rockies and from storm outflows across portions of New Mexico with gusts near or exceeding 50 mph. Despite possible scattered precipitation from thunderstorms, relative humidity values will remain low, between 5-20% for these areas. Across eastern Oregon, western Nevada, and southwest Idaho, breezy west winds will gust to 40 mph, but relative humidity is expected to remain near or above 20% keeping elevated conditions isolated. Rain, with high elevation snow, will continue to move east across the Cascades and become more widespread, affecting large portions of the northern half of the Great Basin, as well as western Montana and Wyoming. In the eastern U.S., scattered showers and thunderstorms will continue to move east across the central Great Plains and the eastern U.S. from the panhandle of Florida northward into the Great Lakes. Dry conditions will persist in the Mid-Atlantic to the Northeast, where portions of the coast between Maryland and Massachusetts will have relative humidity values as low as 22%, with the rest of the region generally above 30%. In Alaska, cool and moist conditions are expected to persist, with scattered light showers across central Alaska. National Predictive Services Outlook (7-Day Significant Fire Potential Outlook) National Weather Service, Storm Prediction Center: Fire Weather Outlook Map and discussion National Weather Service: Fire Weather Hazards Map National Weather Service, Weather Prediction Center: National Forecast Chart and Short Range Forecast Discussion 6 Minutes for Safety topics can be found here.",
